1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,096
Welcome to Unit Eight of Algebra One:
polynomials and factoring.

2
00:00:04,546 --> 00:00:08,926
In this lesson, we'll learn the
vocabulary, and how to add and subtract

3
00:00:08,926 --> 00:00:09,666
polynomials.

4
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:15,915
A polynomial is a sum of terms, where each
term is a number times a variable to a

5
00:00:15,915 --> 00:00:17,115
whole-number power.

6
00:00:17,565 --> 00:00:22,962
One term is a monomial, two terms is a
binomial, and three terms is a trinomial.

7
00:00:24,100 --> 00:00:27,428
Standard form lists the terms from highest
power to lowest.

8
00:00:27,878 --> 00:00:33,122
The degree is the highest power. Three x
squared minus five x plus two has degree

9
00:00:33,122 --> 00:00:35,387
two, and leading coefficient three.

10
00:00:36,533 --> 00:00:38,923
To add polynomials, combine like terms.

11
00:00:39,373 --> 00:00:45,049
Two x squared plus three x minus four,
plus x squared minus five x plus seven.

12
00:00:45,049 --> 00:00:48,397
That's three x squared minus two x plus
three.

13
00:00:49,533 --> 00:00:54,787
To subtract, distribute the minus sign to
every term of the second polynomial, then

14
00:00:54,787 --> 00:00:55,293
combine.

15
00:00:55,743 --> 00:01:01,830
Five x squared plus x minus two, minus the
quantity two x squared minus three x plus

16
00:01:01,830 --> 00:01:07,772
four. That becomes five x squared plus x
minus two, minus two x squared plus three

17
00:01:07,772 --> 00:01:08,714
x minus four.

18
00:01:09,833 --> 00:01:12,841
Combine: three x squared plus four x minus
six.

19
00:01:13,291 --> 00:01:18,219
The most common mistake is changing only
the first sign. Every term must flip.

20
00:01:19,367 --> 00:01:24,828
Your turn. Subtract: four x squared minus
two x plus one, minus the quantity x

21
00:01:24,828 --> 00:01:27,068
squared plus three x minus five.

22
00:01:27,518 --> 00:01:28,969
Pause the video and try it.

23
00:01:29,419 --> 00:01:35,555
Flip every sign: four x squared minus two
x plus one, minus x squared minus three x

24
00:01:35,555 --> 00:01:40,213
plus five. The answer is three x squared
minus five x plus six.

25
00:01:41,333 --> 00:01:45,984
Let's subtract two polynomials, the place
where sign mistakes usually happen.

26
00:01:47,433 --> 00:01:53,227
Simplify five x cubed minus two x squared
plus seven, minus the quantity three x

27
00:01:53,227 --> 00:01:56,414
cubed plus four x squared minus x plus
nine.

28
00:01:57,533 --> 00:02:02,909
Distribute the minus sign to every term in
the second polynomial. Every sign flips.

29
00:02:04,033 --> 00:02:07,916
Combine the x cubed terms: five minus
three is two x cubed.

30
00:02:09,033 --> 00:02:13,790
The x squared terms: negative two minus
four is negative six x squared.

31
00:02:14,933 --> 00:02:16,917
There's only one x term, plus x.

32
00:02:18,066 --> 00:02:21,202
And the constants: seven minus nine is
negative two.

33
00:02:22,333 --> 00:02:27,867
The result is two x cubed minus six x
squared plus x minus two. It's a cubic

34
00:02:27,867 --> 00:02:29,032
with four terms.

35
00:02:30,166 --> 00:02:35,542
Watch out. The minus sign applies to every
term inside the parentheses, not just the

36
00:02:35,542 --> 00:02:40,598
first. Only combine like terms, with the
same variable and power. And write the

37
00:02:40,598 --> 00:02:42,902
answer with the highest power first.

38
00:02:44,033 --> 00:02:49,773
Your turn. Simplify four x squared minus
three x plus one, minus the quantity x

39
00:02:49,773 --> 00:02:54,060
squared minus five x minus six. Pause the
video and try it.

40
00:02:58,600 --> 00:03:02,866
Flip the signs and combine: three x
squared plus two x plus seven.

41
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:08,273
In this lesson, we'll multiply
polynomials, using the distributive

42
00:03:08,273 --> 00:03:09,568
property every time.

43
00:03:10,700 --> 00:03:14,177
To multiply a monomial by a polynomial,
distribute.

44
00:03:14,627 --> 00:03:20,255
Three x times the quantity two x squared
minus x plus four is six x cubed minus

45
00:03:20,255 --> 00:03:22,393
three x squared plus twelve x.

46
00:03:23,533 --> 00:03:28,545
To multiply two binomials, multiply each
term of the first by each term of the

47
00:03:28,545 --> 00:03:28,995
second.

48
00:03:29,445 --> 00:03:36,055
x plus three, times x plus five. x times x
is x squared. x times five is five x.

49
00:03:36,055 --> 00:03:40,517
Three times x is three x. Three times five
is fifteen.

50
00:03:40,967 --> 00:03:44,465
Combine like terms: x squared plus eight x
plus fifteen.

51
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:50,950
An area model keeps it organized. Put one
binomial along the top and the other down

52
00:03:50,950 --> 00:03:51,531
the side.

53
00:03:51,981 --> 00:03:57,385
Fill in each box with a product, then add
the boxes. For two x minus one times x

54
00:03:57,385 --> 00:04:02,722
plus four, the boxes are two x squared,
eight x, negative x, and negative four.

55
00:04:02,722 --> 00:04:05,762
That's two x squared plus seven x minus
four.

56
00:04:06,900 --> 00:04:09,545
The same idea works for bigger
polynomials.

57
00:04:09,995 --> 00:04:16,170
x plus two, times x squared minus x plus
three. Distribute x, then distribute two,

58
00:04:16,170 --> 00:04:20,086
and combine: x cubed plus x squared plus x
plus six.

59
00:04:21,233 --> 00:04:24,561
Quick check: the degree of a product is
the sum of the degrees.

60
00:04:25,011 --> 00:04:27,657
Degree one times degree two gives degree
three.

61
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:32,277
Your turn. Multiply x minus four by x plus
six.

62
00:04:32,727 --> 00:04:34,178
Pause the video and try it.

63
00:04:34,628 --> 00:04:40,523
x squared plus six x minus four x minus
twenty-four, which is x squared plus two x

64
00:04:40,523 --> 00:04:41,817
minus twenty-four.

65
00:04:42,966 --> 00:04:47,126
Here's a worked example of multiplying a
binomial by a trinomial.

66
00:04:48,566 --> 00:04:53,153
Multiply two x minus three by x squared
plus four x minus five.

67
00:04:54,299 --> 00:04:59,803
Distribute two x to every term: two x
cubed plus eight x squared minus ten x.

68
00:05:00,933 --> 00:05:06,245
Distribute negative three: negative three
x squared minus twelve x plus fifteen.

69
00:05:07,366 --> 00:05:08,625
Line up the like terms.

70
00:05:09,766 --> 00:05:14,843
Combine: two x cubed plus five x squared
minus twenty two x plus fifteen.

71
00:05:15,966 --> 00:05:21,235
The product is two x cubed plus five x
squared minus twenty two x plus fifteen.

72
00:05:22,366 --> 00:05:27,673
Watch out. Multiply every term by every
term. Count your products: two terms times

73
00:05:27,673 --> 00:05:32,009
three terms means six products. And carry
each term's sign with it.

74
00:05:33,133 --> 00:05:39,093
Your turn. Multiply x plus two by three x
squared minus x plus four. Pause the video

75
00:05:39,093 --> 00:05:39,874
and try it.

76
00:05:44,399 --> 00:05:50,464
Three x cubed minus x squared plus four x,
plus six x squared minus two x plus eight.

77
00:05:50,464 --> 00:05:54,959
That's three x cubed plus five x squared
plus two x plus eight.

78
00:05:56,100 --> 00:06:00,676
Some products show up so often that it's
worth knowing their patterns. In this

79
00:06:00,676 --> 00:06:02,201
lesson, we'll learn three.

80
00:06:03,333 --> 00:06:08,255
The square of a sum: a plus b, squared,
equals a squared plus two a b plus b

81
00:06:08,255 --> 00:06:08,773
squared.

82
00:06:09,223 --> 00:06:14,365
For example, x plus five, squared, is x
squared plus ten x plus twenty-five.

83
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:20,510
The square of a difference: a minus b,
squared, equals a squared minus two a b

84
00:06:20,510 --> 00:06:21,473
plus b squared.

85
00:06:21,923 --> 00:06:26,787
Three x minus two, squared, is nine x
squared minus twelve x plus four.

86
00:06:27,933 --> 00:06:33,117
A common mistake is to write x plus five
squared as x squared plus twenty-five.

87
00:06:33,567 --> 00:06:38,111
That forgets the middle term. Squaring a
binomial always gives three terms.

88
00:06:39,233 --> 00:06:44,844
The sum times the difference: a plus b,
times a minus b, equals a squared minus b

89
00:06:44,844 --> 00:06:45,399
squared.

90
00:06:45,849 --> 00:06:51,216
The middle terms cancel. x plus seven
times x minus seven is x squared minus

91
00:06:51,216 --> 00:06:51,993
forty-nine.

92
00:06:53,133 --> 00:06:55,821
These patterns also make mental math
faster.

93
00:06:56,271 --> 00:07:01,801
Twenty-one times nineteen is twenty plus
one, times twenty minus one. That's four

94
00:07:01,801 --> 00:07:05,487
hundred minus one, which is three hundred
ninety-nine.

95
00:07:06,633 --> 00:07:09,300
Your turn. Expand two x plus three,
squared.

96
00:07:09,750 --> 00:07:11,201
Pause the video and try it.

97
00:07:11,651 --> 00:07:17,578
Four x squared, plus two times two x times
three, which is twelve x, plus nine. So

98
00:07:17,578 --> 00:07:20,397
four x squared plus twelve x plus nine.

99
00:07:21,533 --> 00:07:24,904
Let's use the special product patterns to
multiply quickly.

100
00:07:26,633 --> 00:07:32,681
Use patterns to multiply three x minus
five, squared, and four y plus seven times

101
00:07:32,681 --> 00:07:34,100
four y minus seven.

102
00:07:35,233 --> 00:07:39,853
For part a, use the square of a
difference: a squared minus two a b plus b

103
00:07:39,853 --> 00:07:40,353
squared.

104
00:07:41,500 --> 00:07:43,334
Here a is three x and b is five.

105
00:07:44,466 --> 00:07:49,544
a squared is nine x squared, two a b is
thirty x, and b squared is twenty five.

106
00:07:50,666 --> 00:07:54,805
For part b, a sum times a difference is a
squared minus b squared.

107
00:07:55,933 --> 00:07:59,858
Sixteen y squared minus forty nine. The
middle terms cancel.

108
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:06,754
Part a is nine x squared minus thirty x
plus twenty five, and part b is sixteen y

109
00:08:06,754 --> 00:08:08,530
squared minus forty nine.

110
00:08:09,666 --> 00:08:14,884
Watch out. A binomial squared is not just
the squares; don't forget the middle term.

111
00:08:14,884 --> 00:08:19,792
Square the coefficient too, so three x
squared is nine x squared. And sum times

112
00:08:19,792 --> 00:08:21,656
difference has no middle term.

113
00:08:22,800 --> 00:08:27,365
Your turn. Multiply two x plus three,
squared. Pause the video and try it.

114
00:08:31,900 --> 00:08:37,020
Four x squared, plus two times two x times
three which is twelve x, plus nine.

115
00:08:38,166 --> 00:08:43,341
Factoring is multiplying in reverse. In
this lesson, we'll start with the greatest

116
00:08:43,341 --> 00:08:44,225
common factor.

117
00:08:45,366 --> 00:08:50,550
Multiplying turns three times the quantity
x plus two into three x plus six.

118
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:56,244
Factoring goes the other way: from three x
plus six back to three times the quantity

119
00:08:56,244 --> 00:08:56,931
x plus two.

120
00:08:58,066 --> 00:09:01,821
The GCF is the largest factor that divides
every term.

121
00:09:02,271 --> 00:09:07,906
For six x cubed plus nine x squared, the
number part is three, and the variable

122
00:09:07,906 --> 00:09:11,401
part is x squared. So the GCF is three x
squared.

123
00:09:12,533 --> 00:09:16,757
Divide each term by the GCF and write
what's left in parentheses.

124
00:09:17,207 --> 00:09:22,712
Six x cubed plus nine x squared equals
three x squared times the quantity two x

125
00:09:22,712 --> 00:09:23,479
plus three.

126
00:09:24,599 --> 00:09:26,498
When there are four terms, try grouping.

127
00:09:26,948 --> 00:09:33,004
x cubed plus three x squared plus two x
plus six. Group the first two and the last

128
00:09:33,004 --> 00:09:37,657
two: x squared times x plus three, plus
two times x plus three.

129
00:09:38,107 --> 00:09:43,404
Now x plus three is common: the quantity x
squared plus two, times the quantity x

130
00:09:43,404 --> 00:09:44,123
plus three.

131
00:09:45,266 --> 00:09:47,485
Always check by multiplying back out.

132
00:09:47,935 --> 00:09:53,418
Three x squared times two x is six x
cubed, and three x squared times three is

133
00:09:53,418 --> 00:09:55,316
nine x squared. It matches.

134
00:09:56,466 --> 00:10:00,242
Your turn. Factor eight x to the fourth
minus twelve x squared.

135
00:10:00,692 --> 00:10:02,143
Pause the video and try it.

136
00:10:02,593 --> 00:10:08,208
The GCF is four x squared. The answer is
four x squared times the quantity two x

137
00:10:08,208 --> 00:10:09,611
squared minus three.

138
00:10:10,733 --> 00:10:15,533
Here's a worked example that factors out a
GCF, then factors by grouping.

139
00:10:16,966 --> 00:10:22,321
Factor completely: six x cubed minus nine
x squared plus four x minus six.

140
00:10:23,466 --> 00:10:28,309
First check for a GCF of all four terms.
There isn't one, so try grouping.

141
00:10:29,433 --> 00:10:31,609
Group the first two terms and the last
two.

142
00:10:32,733 --> 00:10:38,109
Factor three x squared from the first pair
and two from the second. Both leave two x

143
00:10:38,109 --> 00:10:38,877
minus three.

144
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:43,136
Factor out the common binomial, two x
minus three.

145
00:10:44,266 --> 00:10:48,789
The factored form is two x minus three,
times three x squared plus two.

146
00:10:49,933 --> 00:10:54,912
Watch out. Always look for a GCF of all
the terms first. When grouping, both

147
00:10:54,912 --> 00:11:00,219
groups must leave the same binomial; if
they don't, try factoring a negative. And

148
00:11:00,219 --> 00:11:01,922
check by multiplying back.

149
00:11:03,066 --> 00:11:08,619
Your turn. Factor x cubed plus five x
squared minus two x minus ten. Pause the

150
00:11:08,619 --> 00:11:09,829
video and try it.

151
00:11:14,366 --> 00:11:20,264
x squared times x plus five, minus two
times x plus five. That's x plus five

152
00:11:20,264 --> 00:11:22,281
times x squared minus two.

153
00:11:23,400 --> 00:11:28,115
In this lesson, we'll factor trinomials
like x squared plus b x plus c.

154
00:11:29,233 --> 00:11:35,765
When you multiply x plus p by x plus q,
you get x squared plus the quantity p plus

155
00:11:35,765 --> 00:11:37,916
q, times x, plus p times q.

156
00:11:38,366 --> 00:11:42,441
So to factor, find two numbers that
multiply to c and add to b.

157
00:11:43,567 --> 00:11:46,255
Factor x squared plus seven x plus twelve.

158
00:11:46,705 --> 00:11:51,248
We need two numbers that multiply to
twelve and add to seven. Three and four

159
00:11:51,248 --> 00:11:51,547
work.

160
00:11:51,997 --> 00:11:54,579
So it's x plus three, times x plus four.

161
00:11:55,700 --> 00:11:58,431
Factor x squared plus two x minus fifteen.

162
00:11:58,881 --> 00:12:04,483
The product is negative, so one number is
negative. Five and negative three multiply

163
00:12:04,483 --> 00:12:06,817
to negative fifteen and add to two.

164
00:12:07,267 --> 00:12:09,976
So it's x plus five, times x minus three.

165
00:12:11,100 --> 00:12:13,873
Factor x squared minus nine x plus twenty.

166
00:12:14,323 --> 00:12:19,561
The product is positive but the sum is
negative, so both numbers are negative.

167
00:12:19,561 --> 00:12:22,046
Negative four and negative five work.

168
00:12:22,496 --> 00:12:25,355
So it's x minus four, times x minus five.

169
00:12:26,500 --> 00:12:32,038
Sometimes no pair works. For x squared
plus x plus one, no two integers multiply

170
00:12:32,038 --> 00:12:33,561
to one and add to one.

171
00:12:34,011 --> 00:12:36,721
We call that trinomial prime over the
integers.

172
00:12:37,867 --> 00:12:41,131
Your turn. Factor x squared minus x minus
twenty.

173
00:12:41,581 --> 00:12:43,031
Pause the video and try it.

174
00:12:43,481 --> 00:12:49,074
We need a product of negative twenty and a
sum of negative one: negative five and

175
00:12:49,074 --> 00:12:52,249
four. So it's x minus five, times x plus
four.

176
00:12:53,366 --> 00:12:56,545
Let's factor a trinomial where the
constant is negative.

177
00:12:58,466 --> 00:13:01,581
Factor x squared minus four x minus twenty
one.

178
00:13:02,699 --> 00:13:07,543
We need two numbers that multiply to
negative twenty one and add to negative

179
00:13:07,543 --> 00:13:07,862
four.

180
00:13:08,999 --> 00:13:12,455
The product is negative, so the numbers
have opposite signs.

181
00:13:13,599 --> 00:13:17,589
List pairs: one and negative twenty one,
three and negative seven.

182
00:13:18,733 --> 00:13:22,338
Three plus negative seven is negative
four. That's our pair.

183
00:13:23,466 --> 00:13:26,730
So the factors are x plus three and x
minus seven.

184
00:13:27,866 --> 00:13:33,586
x squared minus four x minus twenty one
factors as x plus three times x minus

185
00:13:33,586 --> 00:13:34,031
seven.

186
00:13:35,166 --> 00:13:40,844
Watch out. If c is positive, both numbers
have the same sign as b. If c is negative,

187
00:13:40,844 --> 00:13:46,049
the signs are opposite, and the larger
number takes b's sign. Always check by

188
00:13:46,049 --> 00:13:47,198
multiplying back.

189
00:13:48,333 --> 00:13:53,620
Your turn. Factor x squared plus two x
minus thirty five. Pause the video and try

190
00:13:53,620 --> 00:13:53,815
it.

191
00:13:58,333 --> 00:14:03,934
Seven and negative five multiply to
negative thirty five and add to two. x

192
00:14:03,934 --> 00:14:06,205
plus seven times x minus five.

193
00:14:07,333 --> 00:14:12,025
When the leading coefficient isn't one,
factoring takes one more step. In this

194
00:14:12,025 --> 00:14:14,010
lesson, we'll use the a c method.

195
00:14:15,133 --> 00:14:20,530
Multiply a times c. Then find two numbers
that multiply to a c and add to b.

196
00:14:20,980 --> 00:14:27,094
For two x squared plus seven x plus three,
a c is six. One and six multiply to six

197
00:14:27,094 --> 00:14:28,362
and add to seven.

198
00:14:29,500 --> 00:14:31,740
Use those numbers to split the middle
term.

199
00:14:32,190 --> 00:14:35,155
Two x squared plus x plus six x plus
three.

200
00:14:36,300 --> 00:14:41,681
Now factor by grouping. x times the
quantity two x plus one, plus three times

201
00:14:41,681 --> 00:14:43,638
the quantity two x plus one.

202
00:14:44,088 --> 00:14:47,480
So the answer is two x plus one, times x
plus three.

203
00:14:48,600 --> 00:14:51,373
Factor three x squared minus x minus ten.

204
00:14:51,823 --> 00:14:57,809
a c is negative thirty. Negative six and
five multiply to negative thirty and add

205
00:14:57,809 --> 00:14:58,991
to negative one.

206
00:14:59,441 --> 00:15:05,807
Split: three x squared minus six x plus
five x minus ten. Group: three x times x

207
00:15:05,807 --> 00:15:12,093
minus two, plus five times x minus two.
That's three x plus five, times x minus

208
00:15:12,093 --> 00:15:12,412
two.

209
00:15:13,533 --> 00:15:15,453
Always look for a GCF first.

210
00:15:15,903 --> 00:15:21,589
Four x squared plus fourteen x plus six is
two times the quantity two x squared plus

211
00:15:21,589 --> 00:15:24,500
seven x plus three, which we just
factored.

212
00:15:25,633 --> 00:15:29,238
Your turn. Factor two x squared plus five
x minus three.

213
00:15:29,688 --> 00:15:31,139
Pause the video and try it.

214
00:15:31,589 --> 00:15:37,755
a c is negative six: six and negative one.
Split and group to get two x minus one,

215
00:15:37,755 --> 00:15:39,184
times x plus three.

216
00:15:39,333 --> 00:15:40,333
Next time, we'll factor special products.
If this helped, subscribe to School STEM,

217
00:15:40,333 --> 00:15:45,133
Here's a worked example of the A C method
for a leading coefficient other than one.

218
00:15:46,566 --> 00:15:49,702
Factor six x squared plus seven x minus
five.

219
00:15:50,833 --> 00:15:55,249
Multiply a and c: six times negative five
is negative thirty.

220
00:15:56,366 --> 00:16:01,922
Find two numbers that multiply to negative
thirty and add to seven: ten and negative

221
00:16:01,922 --> 00:16:02,318
three.

222
00:16:03,466 --> 00:16:06,517
Split the middle term: plus ten x minus
three x.

223
00:16:07,666 --> 00:16:13,512
Group and factor: two x times three x plus
five, minus one times three x plus five.

224
00:16:14,633 --> 00:16:16,489
Factor out three x plus five.

225
00:16:17,633 --> 00:16:23,608
Six x squared plus seven x minus five
factors as three x plus five times two x

226
00:16:23,608 --> 00:16:24,374
minus one.

227
00:16:25,500 --> 00:16:30,026
Watch out. Check for a GCF before
starting. Split the middle term using the

228
00:16:30,026 --> 00:16:35,036
pair you found, then group. If the groups
don't match, recheck your pair and signs.

229
00:16:36,166 --> 00:16:41,412
Your turn. Factor three x squared minus
ten x plus eight. Pause the video and try

230
00:16:41,412 --> 00:16:41,606
it.

231
00:16:46,133 --> 00:16:51,716
a c is twenty four. Negative six and
negative four work. The answer is three x

232
00:16:51,716 --> 00:16:53,792
minus four times x minus two.

233
00:16:54,933 --> 00:16:59,680
The special products from Lesson Three
work backward too. In this last lesson of

234
00:16:59,680 --> 00:17:01,994
Unit Eight, we'll factor them on sight.

235
00:17:03,133 --> 00:17:08,379
A difference of squares factors as a
squared minus b squared equals a plus b,

236
00:17:08,379 --> 00:17:09,469
times a minus b.

237
00:17:09,919 --> 00:17:14,399
x squared minus thirty-six is x plus six,
times x minus six.

238
00:17:15,533 --> 00:17:17,645
Look for perfect squares in both terms.

239
00:17:18,095 --> 00:17:23,905
Nine x squared minus twenty-five is three
x squared minus five squared. So it's

240
00:17:23,905 --> 00:17:27,140
three x plus five, times three x minus
five.

241
00:17:28,266 --> 00:17:33,080
A perfect square trinomial has a squared
first term, a squared last term, and a

242
00:17:33,080 --> 00:17:35,456
middle term that's twice their product.

243
00:17:35,906 --> 00:17:42,224
x squared plus ten x plus twenty-five is x
plus five, squared. Four x squared minus

244
00:17:42,224 --> 00:17:45,954
twelve x plus nine is two x minus three,
squared.

245
00:17:47,100 --> 00:17:50,748
Factor completely means keep going until
nothing more factors.

246
00:17:51,198 --> 00:17:56,847
Two x squared minus fifty: first take out
two to get two times x squared minus

247
00:17:56,847 --> 00:18:02,206
twenty-five. Then factor again: two times
x plus five, times x minus five.

248
00:18:03,333 --> 00:18:07,907
Watch out: a sum of squares, like x
squared plus nine, does not factor over

249
00:18:07,907 --> 00:18:08,944
the real numbers.

250
00:18:10,066 --> 00:18:13,586
Your turn. Factor completely: three x
squared minus twelve.

251
00:18:14,036 --> 00:18:15,487
Pause the video and try it.

252
00:18:15,937 --> 00:18:21,449
Take out three: three times x squared
minus four. Then three times x plus two,

253
00:18:21,449 --> 00:18:22,721
times x minus two.

254
00:18:23,866 --> 00:18:28,047
Let's factor completely, using more than
one method on the same problem.

255
00:18:29,466 --> 00:18:32,730
Factor two x to the fourth minus thirty
two completely.

256
00:18:32,866 --> 00:18:35,893
First factor out the GCF, two.

257
00:18:37,033 --> 00:18:41,772
x to the fourth minus sixteen is a
difference of squares: x squared, squared,

258
00:18:41,772 --> 00:18:42,942
minus four squared.

259
00:18:44,066 --> 00:18:48,141
That factors as x squared plus four times
x squared minus four.

260
00:18:49,266 --> 00:18:52,530
But x squared minus four is another
difference of squares.

261
00:18:53,666 --> 00:18:58,080
x squared plus four is a sum of squares,
which doesn't factor over the real

262
00:18:58,080 --> 00:18:58,551
numbers.

263
00:18:59,699 --> 00:19:05,540
Factored completely: two times x squared
plus four, times x plus two, times x minus

264
00:19:05,540 --> 00:19:05,822
two.

265
00:19:06,966 --> 00:19:11,861
Watch out. Factor out the GCF first,
always. Keep going until no factor can be

266
00:19:11,861 --> 00:19:16,694
factored further. And a sum of squares
does not factor over the real numbers.

267
00:19:17,833 --> 00:19:23,176
Your turn. Factor three x cubed minus
twelve x squared plus twelve x completely.

268
00:19:23,176 --> 00:19:24,979
Pause the video and try it.

269
00:19:29,499 --> 00:19:35,523
Take out three x, leaving x squared minus
four x plus four, a perfect square. Three

270
00:19:35,523 --> 00:19:37,627
x times x minus two, squared.

271
00:19:38,766 --> 00:19:42,917
Let's finish Unit Eight with an area
problem that needs multiplying and

272
00:19:42,917 --> 00:19:43,502
