273
00:19:44,933 --> 00:19:50,509
A rectangular garden is ten meters by six
meters. A path of width x surrounds it on

274
00:19:50,509 --> 00:19:55,681
every side. Write the path's area as a
polynomial and factor it. Then, if the

275
00:19:55,681 --> 00:19:58,906
path's area is sixty four square meters,
find x.

276
00:20:00,033 --> 00:20:05,835
The outer rectangle adds x on each side,
so it's ten plus two x by six plus two x.

277
00:20:06,966 --> 00:20:11,403
Multiply: sixty plus twenty x plus twelve
x plus four x squared.

278
00:20:12,533 --> 00:20:17,900
Subtract the garden's sixty square meters.
The path's area is four x squared plus

279
00:20:17,900 --> 00:20:18,762
thirty two x.

280
00:20:19,899 --> 00:20:23,953
Factor out the GCF, four x: four x times x
plus eight.

281
00:20:25,099 --> 00:20:30,084
Setting it equal to sixty four and
dividing by four gives x squared plus

282
00:20:30,084 --> 00:20:32,438
eight x minus sixteen equals zero.

283
00:20:33,566 --> 00:20:39,212
Test easy widths. x equals one gives
thirty six, and x equals two gives eighty.

284
00:20:39,212 --> 00:20:43,571
Sixty four is in between, so x is between
one and two meters.

285
00:20:44,699 --> 00:20:49,429
The path area is four x squared plus
thirty two x, which factors as four x

286
00:20:49,429 --> 00:20:54,670
times x plus eight. For sixty four square
meters, the width is between one and two

287
00:20:54,670 --> 00:20:59,847
meters. In the next unit you'll learn to
find it exactly, about one point six six

288
00:20:59,847 --> 00:21:00,294
meters.

289
00:21:01,433 --> 00:21:06,699
Watch out. The path adds x on both sides,
so each dimension grows by two x. The

290
00:21:06,699 --> 00:21:11,833
path's area is the outer area minus the
inner area. And factoring reveals the

291
00:21:11,833 --> 00:21:13,699
structure of the expression.

292
00:21:14,833 --> 00:21:19,960
Your turn. The garden is eight by five
with a path of width x. Write the path's

293
00:21:19,960 --> 00:21:24,049
